Id: node-dreamomni2
Title: DreamOmni2 -- VAE re-pin, img2img strength, render size
Does: Keeps DreamOmni2's VAE in VRAM for a whole batch instead of only its first image, which is what
 stops every image after the first from crawling. Also gives its Editor node an img2img strength and a
 render size of its own, finds every weight it needs through the renderer's configured model folders, and
 makes the diffusers base (the FLUX.1-Kontext family) a required, selectable input on the Edit Pipeline node
 instead of a hardcoded name -- so the renderer can point it at a bound model like any other loader.
Target: custom_nodes/ComfyUI_RH_DreamOmni2
Source: https://github.com/HM-RunningHub/ComfyUI_RH_DreamOmni2.git
Rev: 0a3e8b54c427c1b2ae18952b27c6853d5c076ff3
Why: Six fixes to the RunningHub DreamOmni2 pack. The load-bearing one is re-pinning the VAE on
 every call: diffusers' maybe_free_model_hooks() reinstalls the cpu-offload hook after each __call__,
 so pinning once protects the first image and nothing after it, and the rest of a batch thrashes over
 PCIe. The others add an img2img strength and a render_width/render_height override to the Editor
 node, resize the source to the generation grid before encoding, and widen proj_method to the full
 quant method list. Every weight is asked for by KIND through ComfyUI's own folder_paths -- the Kontext
 pipeline from the diffusers folder, the instruction VLM from text_encoders, the two adapters from loras --
 rather than the absolute paths this was written with, or a search for them. The sixth turns the base
 pipeline's hardcoded FLUX.1-Kontext-dev into a required base_model combo input on the Edit Pipeline node
 (listing the diffusers directories on disk), so the renderer selects the base like any other model slot;
 the Gen pipeline keeps the built-in default, and the Edit node rejects a missing input rather than
 silently falling back.
---
